{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793554440,"nonce":"BLRIgyS3JDpGVnEsfJo3DXh5J5o=","title":"Slider: CSS-first port, bindable disabled","message":"cn::slider chooses its track, fill and thumb colours and its disabled look from ColorToken at build time (style!, inline bg/border, cn-slider-thumb--disabled), moves the thumb on a spring, and keeps drag/hover flags on use_state_keyed. Its .disabled(..) is a build-time bool because the look depends on it.\n\nDo: port to ashui's slider: parts with classes, disabled as a bound attribute, every colour a rule, the thumb positioned by a bound property (as the number gauge's fill is) with any easing a CSS transition on tokens; then .disabled(impl IntoReactive\u003cbool\u003e). Internal flags become use_signal_keyed.\n\nashui first: Slider.hx and the .ui-slider rules in components/css/components.css; the number gauge port (crates/blinc_cn/src/components/number_gauge.rs) for the bound-flex fill pattern.\n\nPart of e4d2db3 and 6d0ea68.","files":null}]}